|~ What is declared under `::fail`, the step `!|` runs on an error
   alone: its constructor and its refusals, each told in one order: the
   refusal and its page, which repairs the step, its facts, its laws. ~|

:fail/construct
  |~~ The step `!| step` from the quote of its step. ~~|
  ::builtin{}

:fail/PayloadNotQuoteError
  |~~ The payload of `::fail` is the quote of the step it wraps, so
      `~(/kind) | tag ::fail` is the step `!| /kind`.
      ::link~(::fail | doc)
  ~~|

:fail/PayloadNotQuoteError/refusesANumber
  |~~ A number payload is refused. ~~|
  ::law~(42 | tag ::fail !| [type /actualType] | eq [::fail/PayloadNotQuoteError ::number])

:fail/PayloadNotQuoteError/buildsTheStepOfAStep
  |~~ The quote of a step builds the step the fail track runs. ~~|
  ::law~(~(/kind) | tag ::fail | [/] | tag ::quote | eq ~(!| /kind))

:fail/ReadBackDiffersError
  |~~ The `::fail` prints as text that reads back as another step, or as
      none, and `:printed` is that text: it wraps one step, so a pipeline
      prints as `!| a | b`, where `!|` takes the first step alone, and an
      empty quote as no step. A pipeline under `!|` is written as a group,
      `~((/kind | print)) | tag ::fail` the step `!| (/kind | print)`.
      ::link~(::fail | doc)
  ~~|

:fail/ReadBackDiffersError/printed
  |~~ The text the step prints as, which reads back as another step or as none. ~~|
  ::string

:fail/ReadBackDiffersError/refusesAPipelineOutsideAGroup
  |~~ A pipeline wrapped without a group prints as text that reads back as two steps. ~~|
  ::law~(~(a | b) | tag ::fail !| [type /printed] | eq [::fail/ReadBackDiffersError "!| a | b"])

:fail/ReadBackDiffersError/refusesAnEmptyQuote
  |~~ An empty quote prints as text that reads back as no step. ~~|
  ::law~(~() | tag ::fail !| [type /printed] | eq [::fail/ReadBackDiffersError "!| "])

:fail/ReadBackDiffersError/wrapsAPipelineInAGroup
  |~~ A pipeline in a group is the one step the fail track runs. ~~|
  ::law~(~((/kind | print)) | tag ::fail | [/] | tag ::quote | eq ~(!| (/kind | print)))
